 * Every other Mach message the process sends, except to the kernel. The trap's
 * registers hold the header: x1 options (0x1 send, 0x100000000 vector,
 * 0x200000000 kernel call), x2 bits | size << 32, x3 remote | local port << 32,
 * x4 voucher | msgh_id << 32. CoreIPC uses msgh_id 0xdba0dba and 0xdba1dba.
 * One line with wall time, thread, port, msgh_id, size, the right the message is
 * sent to (18 for a send-once right) and the channel's label, or - for none.
 */
